# Kconfig file used with conf/mconf/qconf -u <thisfile> for doing implicit
# unselects. This file will contain the name of selectee symbols that need
# to be unselected to the same value of the selector. Example:
#
# config A
#   bool "A - selector"
#   select B
#
# config B
#   bool "B - selectee"
#
# If B is present in this file then it will fall under the 'implicit unselect'
# rule: B = A all the time. Otherwise if B is not in this file then default 
# behaviour applies: B is independent of A except when A = 1 then B=1.
# The symbols in this file are the same as they are in defconfig minus
# CONFIG_. Lines in this file with # as the first char, no preceeding chars,
#  are comments and ignored
#
# ###################################################
# menuhide feature: you can hide menus and all of it's decendents by including
# the exact prompt string appended with " menuhide" to this file. Example:
# to hide the kernel menu whose menu prompt is "Kernel Configuration" add to
# this file:
# Kernel Configuration menuhide
#
# note if you use qconf you can reveal hidden menus as grey options if you 
# turn on Option->Show All Options. Turning this off will complete hide
#
